entative15230714 (one proximal PUM2 interval retained) and15230826 (all four removed) remains useful but is not demonstrated functional escape. miR29-site loss cannot be equated with complete PUM2 escape. Full-length linkage, cluster microheterogeneity, binding-versus-regulation and context limitations remain unchanged. No new assay, rerun, artifact re-registration or courtesy follow-up is warranted. The later request still appears pending in the service inbox; no request state was edited and no waiting loop started.\n \n ## Translation-denominator coordination review\n*** End Patch"}, "timestamp": 1791246157645}
